 height=\"4\" fill=\"#2B3034\"/><path d=\"M374 107 L376 97 L388 97 L388 107 Z\" fill=\"#2B3034\"/><rect x=\"140\" y=\"102\" width=\"94\" height=\"17\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#4A5156\"/><rect x=\"150\" y=\"99\" width=\"78\" height=\"4\" fill=\"#8C959B\"/><rect x=\"160\" y=\"100\" width=\"2\" height=\"2\" fill=\"#2B3034\"/><rect x=\"210\" y=\"100\" width=\"2\" height=\"2\" fill=\"#2B3034\"/><rect x=\"176\" y=\"105\" width=\"36\" height=\"8\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"#2B3034\"/><rect x=\"130\" y=\"119\" width=\"22\" height=\"6\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#2B3034\"/><circle cx=\"146\" cy=\"122\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\"/><rect x=\"131\" y=\"117.5\" width=\"9\" height=\"9\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#D8B23A\" stroke=\"#2B3034\" stroke-width=\".8\"/><path d=\"M158 141 Q156 160 176 160 L196 160 Q204 160 204 141\" stroke=\"#2B3034\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M178 141 Q183 150 176 156\" stroke=\"#2B3034\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"231\" y=\"139\" width=\"4\" height=\"9\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#D8B23A\"/><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"158\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2B3034\"/><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"138\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#2B3034\"/></g><rect x=\"250\" y=\"120\" width=\"40\" height=\"22\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"240\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"309.0\" y2=\"110.0\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M320 110 L309.0 104.0 L309.0 116.0z\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"200\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">oil</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">Oily cloth on metal, remove excess.</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"258\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">PROVE it unloaded. Magazine out.</text></svg>\n<figcaption><b>5.</b> Thin oil on metal. Wipe off the excess.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>Always from the chamber end <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Brush all the way through before you pull back <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the manual's words</summary><ul><li>Few or no shots: \"clean the barrel and cartridge chamber with a clean patch attached to the cleaning rod. Repeat the cleaning, changing patches, until the last patch comes out clean\" (95%, CZ manual page 9).</li><li>Very dirty: \"apply a gun cleaning solution using cleaning brush. Let the solvent act for about 10 minutes ... Then thoroughly scrub out the barrel\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Then \"dry the barrel and cartridge chamber with a clean patch and check that all powder residues, or fouling have been removed\" (95%, page 10).</li><li>\"The cleaning rod and the brush must be inserted into the barrel from the chamber, to prevent wear or damage to the muzzle. Pass the brush all the way through the barrel before reversing the movement. If you try to change directions with the brush in the barrel, the brush could stick\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>The bolt comes out first: chapter 8.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 356\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Five CZ cleaning rules: 1 bore cleaner is for the barrel and chamber only; 2 not on other parts, it can stay in the joints and cause corrosion; 3 other parts get a dry cloth, an old toothbrush, a copper brush or a wooden scraper; 4 before shooting, pull one dry patch through the bore; 5 in very cold weather remove the oil or use a lubricant made for low temperatures.\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"356\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Five cleaning rules</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"44\" width=\"372\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"36\" cy=\"69\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">1</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Bore cleaner</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Barrel and chamber only</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"102\" width=\"372\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"36\" cy=\"127\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">2</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#FF6A13\">Not on other parts</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"143\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">It can sit in joints and rust them</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"160\" width=\"372\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"36\" cy=\"185\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">3</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Other parts</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"201\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Cloth, old toothbrush, copper brush, wood scraper</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"218\" width=\"372\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"36\" cy=\"243\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">4</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"239\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Before shooting</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"259\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">One dry patch through the bore</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"276\" width=\"372\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"36\" cy=\"301\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"306\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">5</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"297\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#FF6A13\">Very cold</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"317\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Remove oil or use a low temperature lube</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"344\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">CZ manual, pages 9 and 10 (95%).</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Bore cleaner stays in the bore <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>One dry patch before shooting <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the rules in full</summary><ul><li>Other parts: \"a dry cloth, old toothbrush, copper bristle brush or a wooden scraper. Preserving oil or paraffin oil can be used ... Never use the agent designed for barrel bore cleaning! These solutions could remain in the joints, and after some time could cause corrosion\" (95%, CZ manual page 10).</li><li>Check no cloth threads or bristles stay in the action <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Stock: a dry cloth or furniture polish <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Preserve: wipe clean, dry parts with an oily cloth or spray, remove all excess, and \"Before shooting always pull through the barrel with dry patch\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Cold: \"At very low temperatures remove the oil from all accessible parts or apply a lubricant especially for these conditions\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Long storage in severe climates: thick preserving grease, removed fully before use <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>When</th><th>Do</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>At the truck</td><td>Unload, PROVE, wipe dry, case it open or loose (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>At home</td><td>Bolt out, dry everything, patch the bore, light oil <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Next day</td><td>Check for rust spots on screws and the muzzle (Tip)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>A wet case holds water against steel (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more wet weather care</summary><ul><li>CZ: clean \"if you get your rifle wet\" (95%, page 9).</li><li>Wood stocks: let them dry slowly at room temperature, not by a heater (Tip).</li><li>Condensation, cold and storage: <a href=\"#/s/firearm-care\">firearm care</a>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Kit</th><th>Price CAD</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Entry</td><td>Pull through bore cord for .22 plus cloth and oil</td><td><span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span></td></tr><tr><td>Mid</td><td>One piece coated .22 rod, jag, bronze brush, patches</td><td><span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span></td></tr><tr><td>Premium</td><td>Rod guide plus the mid kit</td><td><span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Price checked 2026-10-23: no Canadian price confirmed (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why these</summary><ul><li>A one piece coated rod with a bore guide protects the chamber end and the crown (Tip).</li><li>Pull through cords are fast in the field (Tip). CZ's own text describes rod, patch and brush cleaning <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>US listings for Otis .22 kits ran about US$20 to US$40 (60%, search previews 2026-10-23). Canadian prices: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> at your shop.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 356\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Five CZ cleaning rules: 1 bore cleaner is for the barrel and chamber only; 2 not on other parts, it can stay in the joints and cause corrosion; 3 other parts get a dry cloth, an old toothbrush, a copper brush or a wooden scraper; 4 before shooting, pull one dry patch through the bore; 5 in very cold weather remove the oil or use a lubricant made for low temperatures.\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"356\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Five cleaning rules</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"44\" width=\"372\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"36\" cy=\"69\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">1</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"65\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Bore cleaner</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"85\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Barrel and chamber only</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"102\" width=\"372\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"36\" cy=\"127\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">2</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#FF6A13\">Not on other parts</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"143\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">It can sit in joints and rust them</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"160\" width=\"372\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"36\" cy=\"185\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">3</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"181\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Other parts</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"201\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Cloth, old toothbrush, copper brush, wood scraper</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"218\" width=\"372\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"36\" cy=\"243\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">4</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"239\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Before shooting</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"259\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">One dry patch through the bore</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"276\" width=\"372\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"36\" cy=\"301\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"36\" y=\"306\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">5</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"297\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#FF6A13\">Very cold</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"317\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Remove oil or use a low temperature lube</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"344\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">CZ manual, pages 9 and 10 (95%).</text></svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout rule\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): Put it away cleaner than you took it out.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Pushing the rod in from the muzzle and nicking the crown.</li><li>Reversing the brush halfway down the bore.</li><li>Bore solvent on the trigger and bolt, where it sits and rusts.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>After the next wet hunt: run the 5 steps the same night. Time yourself.</p></aside>","<ul><li>CZ 457 manual pages 2, 9 and 10 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Tikka rimfire wax note <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. Kit tips and prices (Tip, <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>). Checked 2026-10-23.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://czubpimstorage.blob.core.windows.net/strapi-pim/assets/735342000443_CZ_457_05_2025_en_es_cs_de_fr_8dc25ceb9d.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CZ 457 instruction manual, 05 2025 (PDF)</a>: page 2 (rule 8), page 9 (when to clean, barrel and chamber), page 10 (direction, other parts, preservation, low temperatures). Read directly 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://media.sako.global/image/upload/v1691658741/Tikka_T1x_T3x_Instruction_Manual_v5.3_cjggnu.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Tikka T1x and T3x manual v5.3</a>: .22 LR wax and cold rounds note, via <a href=\"#/s/rimfire-22\">the .22 rimfire</a> <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Otis .22 kit US prices: search previews of US retailers 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li></ul></details>"]